  "interpretation_rules": [
    "Observed allocated-byte values are qualification measurements, not filesystem-independent upper bounds.",
    "A capacity profile is valid only for the exact repository_id and repository_sha named in the observation.",
    "An unknown repository SHA must not inherit a measured byte prediction from an older SHA as a capacity guarantee.",
    "Archive logical bytes and materialized entries from C0-F2 are separate planning inputs and are not substitutes for allocated-byte measurements.",
    "C0-F1 phase grouping and C0-F3 checkpoint semantics remain mandatory when any future policy consumes these observations.",
    "No fixed percentage, reserve size, refusal threshold or production NO_SPACE behavior is selected by this evidence manifest.",
    "C0-M2 and C0-M3 state-root frontiers are environment-specific qualification observations; they strengthen reserve rationale but do not themselves select a reserve.",
    "State-root reserve policy must remain separate from total Control DB size because M2/M3 observed a stable transaction-headroom frontier while database allocation increased materially.",
    "C0-M2 sidecar sensitivity shows that a pre-existing 32 KiB SQLite SHM sidecar can reduce additional transaction headroom; admission must use the cold-sidecar/worst-case baseline rather than assuming warm sidecars."
  ],
